# MORE at the console (make test-more-keys): a page of LONG.TXT at a time,
# then the rest after a key: a letter; an extended key (F1, 0 then its scan
# code), of which MORE reads both bytes, so the next page waits for a key
# too; Enter and the space bar. The same from a pipe; then ^C at the
# prompt, which ends MORE. The screens are MS-DOS 4.00's MORE's (make
# more-expect). The hard disk is not used.
disk 10M
unchanged
wait A:\\>
type MORE <LONG.TXT
key ret
screen page1
key a
screen page2
key f1
screen page3
key ret
screen page4
key spc
screen end
type TYPE LONG.TXT | MORE
key ret
screen pipe1
key shift-a
screen pipe2
key ctrl-c
screen break
quit
